{"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumSpanningTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:13SpanningTrees0A6ForestV","text":"SpanningForest","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/SpanningForest"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s18AdditiveArithmeticP","text":"AdditiveArithmetic","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","text":"Comparable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Edges are ordered by weight, then by position in "},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Under that order the minimum"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spanning forest is unique, and this is it. Its edges are listed in nondecreasing weight"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and, among equal weights, in position order, and the weight is added up in that order."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Sparse graphs (fewer than 4 edges per vertex) run Kruskal’s algorithm; denser ones run"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Prim’s under the same order and sort the edges taken."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives each edge’s weight from its position, so parallel edges can differ. It is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"called once for each edge that is not a self-loop and is not kept. Negative, zero and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"infinite weights are ordinary weights. A NaN weight traps; filter such edges out first.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(m log m).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Complexity","type":"aside"},{"style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No weight is NaN; the sum of the chosen weights, in the order listed, does"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not overflow and is not NaN."}]}],"name":"Precondition","type":"aside"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"A minimum spanning forest: one minimum spanning tree per connected component.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumspanningtree(weight:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumSpanningTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SpanningForest","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SpanningTrees0A6ForestV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"SpanningTrees"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","title":"minimumSpanningTree(weight:)","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P13SpanningTreesE07minimumC4Tree6weightAD0C6ForestVyxqd__Gqd__5Edges_5IndexQZXE_ts18AdditiveArithmeticRd__SLRd__lF","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpanningTrees\/Kruskal.swift#L21","fileName":"Kruskal.swift"},"role":"symbol"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumSpanningTree(weight:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees/GraphProtocols":{"url":"\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/graphprotocols","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"title":"GraphProtocols","role":"collection","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols"},"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees/SpanningForest":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"SpanningForest","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SpanningForest","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/spanningforest","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A spanning forest of an undirected graph: one spanning tree per connected component, as edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"positions in the graph’s "},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", with the sum of their weights."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/SpanningForest","title":"SpanningForest"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Edges-swift.associatedtype":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl","text":"Collection"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"Edges","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph\/edges-swift.associatedtype","type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype"},"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees":{"kind":"symbol","title":"SpanningTrees","abstract":[],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/spanningtrees","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees"},"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumSpanningTree(weight:)":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumSpanningTree(weight:)","title":"minimumSpanningTree(weight:)","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumspanningtree(weight:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A minimum spanning forest: one minimum spanning tree per connected component."}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumSp